// Views are LikeC4's renderer's; loam reads the model and never a view
// (docs/DESIGN.md rule 26). Three scoped views rather than one `include *`,
// and the scoping is not taste: computing a view is superlinear in the number
// of edges, and one view over 70 boxes and 403 edges is both the slow one to
// draw and the one nobody can read. `core` alone is 271 of those edges.
//
// No `dynamic view` is declared, and that absence is a finding about the
// PRODUCT rather than an omission here: a use case is a call sequence between
// services, and loam is one process. The nearest true statement — "the user
// types `loam validate`, cli calls commands/validate, which calls fourteen
// core packages" — is a call STACK, and a stack drawn as a sequence diagram
// would be an artifact that exists only to make the use-case checks fire.
// ROADMAP's exit criterion 2 forbids exactly that, so the whole `usecase.*`
// family is silent here, and silent because nothing asked.
views {
  view layers {
    title 'loam — entry, commands, core'
    include loam, loam.cli, loam.core, loam.commands, loam.cli -> loam.commands
  }

  view commands {
    title 'loam — what each command reaches into'
    include loam.commands, loam.commands.*, loam.cli, loam.cli -> loam.commands.*
  }

  view core {
    title 'loam — the core DAG'
    include loam.core, loam.core.*
  }
}
